(WEEKLY STEDE TIMETABLE) Tj T*
(Monday: Mathematics examples + Computer concepts/coding; review 10 MCQs.) Tj T*
(Tuesday: Physics concepts/numericals + English grammar/writing.) Tj T*
(Wednesday: Mathematics exercise + Urdu text/writing; review 5 short answers.) Tj T*
(Thursday: Computer theory/logic + Physics derivations; review mistakes.) Tj T*
(Friday: Compulsory subject rotation + elective \(if selected\); revise definitions.) Tj T*
(Saturday: Timed mixed practice + weakest topic; mark your own work.) Tj T*
(Sunday: Light revision/rest; plan next week and update the tracker.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(HOW TO REVISE) Tj T*
(1. Study one small topic for 25-40 minutes.) Tj T*
(2. Close the book and write what you remember.) Tj T*
(3. Solve questions without copying a worked solution.) Tj T*
(4. Check answers and record exactly what went wrong.) Tj T*
(5. Revisit difficult work after 2 days and again after 1 week.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ORIGINAL SELF-TEST PROMPTS) Tj T*
(Maths: Solve one exercise question twice, once with notes and once without.) Tj T*
(Physics: State one law, write its equation, define symbols and give SI units.) Tj T*
(Computer: Write an algorithm for an everyday task; list inputs, steps and outputs.) Tj T*
(English: Write a 150-word paragraph about consistent study and proofread it.) Tj T*
(Urdu: Explain a prescribed lesson or poem using your textbook.) Tj T*
(Economics: Explain one concept with a definition and a daily-life example.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These prompts are original practice starters, not copied board questions.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
